---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JournalList from '../components/JournalList.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { corpus } from '../data/corpus';

const entries = (await getCollection('journal')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const published = corpus.filter((record) => record.state === 'Published').length;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research"
  description="The Restless research record separates observed findings, product direction and unresolved questions."
  active="research"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <h1>A theory that has<br /><em>to survive contact.</em></h1>
    <p>Restless treats organisation design as an empirical question. A useful outcome can change a product decision. A failed evaluation can change how much confidence the outcome deserves.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="research-principles">
    <article><h2>Direction</h2><p>Authority stays deterministic at the external boundary. Files remain the primary work primitive. Native outcomes are the first review surface.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Evidence</h2><p>Current defaults are scoped by model, workload and evidence. They are not converted into universal rules.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Unknowns</h2><p>Unresolved questions remain visible. A quiet system may be correct when there is no decision-changing work to do.</p></article>
  </section>

  <section class="corpus-callout">
    <div><strong>{published} of {corpus.length}</strong><p>material experiment records have a public article home.</p></div>
    <p>One result remains deferred because the EXP-07 blind owner decision and arm identity are sealed. The corpus map explains the boundary.</p>
    <a href="/research/corpus/">Inspect corpus coverage <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="journal-preview">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2>Current research record</h2><p>Each note names its thesis, its evidence and where the conclusion stops.</p></div>
    <JournalList entries={entries} />
  </section>

  <section class="open-questions">
    <h2>The next questions have to earn their machinery.</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>What observed signal shows that a coherent outcome has exceeded one worker's effective session?</li>
      <li>When does a bounded parallel hand become Staff responsibility?</li>
      <li>Which native artifact and event boundaries transfer beyond code?</li>
      <li>Can real external signals reach the accountable owner without turning Exec into a relay?</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
